@notice Emitted per member that failed its epoch verdict, whether or not a stamp
         followed. A verdict without a stamp is the normal case: the correlation guard
         fired, the per-close cap was spent, or no replacement existed.

@notice Emitted when the stipend leg of a close fails. The liveness leg has already
         committed by then — a frozen payment is preferred to any chance of a frozen
         chain. The cursor does not advance, so the next close retries contiguously.

@notice Record one block's producer. Injected once per block by the executor.
 @param blockNumber EVM `block.number` of the current block (idempotency key). NOT
        trusted as an epoch tag — the epoch is derived from it, because the block number
        is deterministic over agreed state while a proposer-supplied tag is not.
 @param leaderIndex The producer's position in the epoch committee, already checked at
        vote time against the consensus-supplied round leader.

@notice The epoch at whose close `validator` is released, or 0 when not excluded.
         Read by governance activation so re-activating a validator cannot silently
         cancel a pending exclusion.
